ntially and can only pay attention to the words in the sentence that it has=
 already translated (so, only the words before the word currently being gen=
erated). For example, when we have predicted the first three words of the t=
ranslated target, we give them to the decoder  which then uses all the inpu=
ts of the encoder to try to predict the fourth word.</p> <p data-svelte-h=
=3D"svelte-pjyju0">To speed things up during training (when the model has a=
ccess to target sentences), the decoder is fed the whole target, but it is =
not allowed to use future words (if it had access to the word at position 2=
